  "policy_sha256": "84f656b16099dcb248866f714453e5bd3e275bdb5d4929c4fad838ee8b29ed2c",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00001",
      "text": "More than forty poets from across Myanmar participated in a poetry reading event in Yangon City aimed at expressing support to displaced Rohingya minority. They were joined by several Rohingya writers who recited poems through a Skype video from their refugee camp in Cox's Bazar, Bangladesh.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "body_start": 0,
      "body_end": 292,
      "source_links": [
        "http://www.mizzima.com/article/refugee-writers-dial-myanmar-poetry-slam"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00002",
      "text": "The ‘Poetry for Humanity’ themes event was a small cultural activity with national symbolic importance. Myanmar has more than one hundred ethnic groups but the government has refused to recognize the Rohingya people, who are mostly Muslims living in the northwestern state of Rakhine. In recent years, communal clashes erupted in Rakhine involving some Rohingya and Buddhist hardliners. The conflict reflected the discrimination against the Rohingya who are treated as illegal immigrants by state institutions.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 2,
      "body_start": 294,
      "body_end": 804,
      "source_links": [
        "https://globalvoices.org/specialcoverage/2012-special-coverage/rohingya-myanmar-burma/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00003",
      "text": "Since 2017, more than 700,000 Rohingya residents have fled their homes to escape the fighting between government troops and the Arakan Rohingya Salvation Army. Many fled to the neighboring country of Bangladesh.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 3,
      "body_start": 806,
      "body_end": 1017,
      "source_links": [
        "https://globalvoices.org/2017/08/29/thousands-of-rohingya-fleeing-violence-are-stranded-on-the-bangladesh-myanmar-border/",
        "https://globalvoices.org/2017/09/23/myanmar-government-vows-to-address-refugee-crisis-in-rakhine-state-but-avoids-saying-rohingya/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00004",
      "text": "On 23 January 2020, the International Court of Justice ordered Myanmar to implement measures against genocide based on a case filed by Gambia.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 4,
      "body_start": 1019,
      "body_end": 1161,
      "source_links": [
        "https://twitter.com/CIJ_ICJ/status/1220306320529788928"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00005",
      "text": "In light of this global court ruling, the poetry event held on 25-26 January should be seen as a courageous act of solidarity with the Rohingya minority. It is also noteworthy to mention that organizers adopted the name Rohingya in the event, instead of the pejorative ‘Bengali’ label which many Burmese officials use to indicate that the Rohingya are illegal immigrants.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 5,
      "body_start": 1163,
      "body_end": 1534,
      "source_links": [
        "https://globalvoices.org/2016/05/29/myanmar-wants-the-world-to-stop-using-the-word-rohingya-for-persecuted-ethnic-group/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00006",
      "text": "But instead of directly commenting on government policies or court rulings, the participants demonstrated how ethnic groups can unite despite the diversity of cultures in the country.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 6,
      "body_start": 1536,
      "body_end": 1719,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00007",
      "text": "Mayyu Ali, a Rohingya poet in the Cox's Bazar camp, emphasized that he and other refugees consider themselves to be part of Myanmar:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 7,
      "body_start": 1721,
      "body_end": 1853,
      "source_links": [
        "https://twitter.com/AliMayyu/status/1221053487858872324"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00008",
      "text": "> All we want our Burmese brothers & sisters is to feel us, we #Rohingya also love our #Myanmar & adore our Burmese literature.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 8,
      "body_start": 1855,
      "body_end": 1982,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00009",
      "text": "> Building bridge between different communities through poetry.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 9,
      "body_start": 1984,
      "body_end": 2047,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00010",
      "text": "> We’ve strong tradition of poetry movement since colonial era.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 10,
      "body_start": 2049,
      "body_end": 2112,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00011",
      "text": "Reactions on Twitter celebrated the success of the event in proving that Buddhists, the Rohingya, and other ethnic minorities can show love and support for each other in a single event.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 11,
      "body_start": 2114,
      "body_end": 2299,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00012",
      "text": "A poem by another Rohingya poet Azad Mohammed was also featured in the event",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 12,
      "body_start": 2301,
      "body_end": 2377,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-695792-b00013",
      "text": "Yanghee Lee, the UN Special Rapporteur on Myanmar, also praised the event.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 13,
      "body_start": 2379,
      "body_end": 2453,
      "source_links": [
        "https://twitter.com/YangheeLeeSKKU/status/1221646625182928896"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    }
  ],
